Hello,

after some weeks of stressing my Miata, i am finally finished building all
packages i need, and some more, which some of you might want to have :)

The complete base OS including XFree86 and all those packages can be downloaded
here:

http://www.atlas.uni-wuppertal.de/netbsd/

Thanks to Torsten Harenberg for providing the space and bandwith for this. To
avoid useless waste of traffic, please think of the following:

- Everything needs at least a 21164A CPU. No AlphaStation 200, no Multias, you
  can safely ignore every machine below 433MHz. These builds are optimized
  for this CPU in a way that it needs BWX extensions. It's senseless to
  download everything without having at least a 21164A CPU.

- Don't wget the whole directory. There are symlinks, which means you get all
  packages at least twice, as HTTP doesn't know about symlinks and resolves
  them, delivering the file again. I leave the symlinks in for better
  searching.

- If you want everything, download netbsd.tar and packages.tar.

- Make sure to consult the README.TXT!

- look at the directory releases/2.0/alpha-21164a/misc for some files you may
  want to use if building more packages or using my kernel as a base for your
  own. There also are some patches and a manually built xca.

So, hope there are some people who can use this stuff. Bug reports may be sent
to me. No bugs in the application, but completely non-working packages or other
issues may be told to me.

Have fun with this.

...Michael

